Third-party machine learning models bundled with this application
=================================================================

The model weights in this directory are not our own work. They are redistributed
here unmodified in content — only repacked, in that the upstream weight shards
were concatenated into a single .bin per model and the `weightsManifest` in each
model.json was rewritten to point at it. Numerical output is bit-identical to the
upstream files.

MobileNet v4 is the one exception: it was never published as a TensorFlow.js model, so
those two directories hold a conversion of the ONNX export of the original timm
weights, not a repack. The graph is numerically equivalent to that export — the
classifier head was cut off, nothing was retrained or quantised. See
docs/mobilenet-v4-conversion.md, scripts/convert-mobilenet-v4.py for the conversion and
scripts/verify-mobilenet-v4.mjs for the check that keeps it honest.

See PROVENANCE.json for the exact source URL, retrieval date and SHA-256 of every
file, and scripts/vendor-models.mjs for the script that downloaded them.

Why these are vendored rather than fetched at runtime: the upstream host
tfhub.dev now redirects to kaggle.com, and that redirect chain does not answer
browser fetches (HTTP 403, no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header). Self-hosting
is therefore required for the models to load at all, and it additionally lets the
application run in filtered school networks and offline.

